  "rationale": "The webpage content is entirely focused on the SEC's enforcement results for fiscal year 2024, which directly addresses the user's request for 'SEC enforcement results FY2024'. However, the content does not contain any information about NERC enforcement actions or Flagstar settlement details. Therefore, the extracted information is limited to the SEC FY2024 results.",
  "evidence": "The SEC announced that it filed 583 total enforcement actions in fiscal year 2024 while obtaining orders for $8.2 billion in financial remedies, the highest amount in SEC history. The 583 enforcement actions represent a 26 percent decline in total enforcement actions compared to fiscal year 2023. Of those cases, the Commission filed 431 “stand-alone” actions (14 percent less than prior year), 93 “follow-on” administrative proceedings (43 percent less), and 59 actions against issuers delinquent in filings (51 percent decrease). The $8.2 billion consisted of $6.1 billion in disgorgement and prejudgment interest (also highest on record) and $2.1 billion in civil penalties (second-highest). Approximately 56 percent of the $8.2 billion is attributable to a monetary judgment against Terraform Labs and Do Kwon. The SEC obtained orders barring 124 individuals from serving as officers and directors, the second-highest number in a decade. The SEC distributed $345 million to harmed investors in FY2024, and over $2.7 billion since FY2021. It received 45,130 tips, complaints, and referrals (most ever), including more than 24,000 whistleblower tips, and issued whistleblower awards totaling $255 million. The content also details proactive initiatives such as off-channel communications (over $600 million in penalties against 70+ firms), Marketing Rule cases, whistleblower protection cases (including $18 million penalty against J.P. Morgan), and insider/manager disclosure failures. Major fraud cases include Terraform Labs ($4.5 billion), Morgan Stanley ($249 million), FirstEnergy ($100 million), SAP ($98 million), and Macquarie ($79.8 million). Emerging technology cases cover AI, relationship investment scams, cybersecurity, and crypto. Individual accountability actions include Do Kwon ($200 million+), former Silvergate executives, and others. The SEC also conducted five trials and obtained favorable verdicts, including the first crypto-related trial (SEC v. Terraform Labs) and the first insider trading case based on a peer company (SEC v. Panuwat).",
  "summary": "The SEC's fiscal year 2024 enforcement results include 583 total actions (down 26% from FY2023) and a record $8.2 billion in financial remedies, driven largely by the $4.5 billion Terraform Labs judgment. The SEC also obtained 124 officer-and-director bars, distributed $345 million to investors, and received a record 45,130 tips. Notable initiatives include recordkeeping penalties exceeding $600 million, Marketing Rule enforcement, and whistleblower protection cases. The content does not mention any NERC enforcement actions or Flagstar settlement details."
